// SR 641.711 — Chapter 7a Crediting of Reduction Effect of Renewable Thermal and Motor Fuels
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
Inserted by No I of the O of 2 April 2025, in force since 1 May 2025 (AS 2025 248).
|

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:PATH
Section 1 Principles
|

:INFO
Art. 92c
1 The reduction effect of renewable thermal and motor fuels and low-emission aviation fuels can be credited as part of a measure under the CO2 Act provided that:
a. the thermal or motor fuels meet the requirements of the Ordinance of 2 April 2025 on the Placing on the Market of Renewable and Low-Emission Thermal and Motor Fuels (RFO); and
b. there is a guarantee of origin in accordance with Section 2a EnO assigned to the said measure under the CO2 Act.
2 For installation operators and aircraft operators, the guarantee of origin is assigned to the said measure by the supplier of the thermal or motor fuel.
|

:NOTE
Para. 1 let. a — SR 814.311.1
Para. 1 let. b — SR 730.01

:PATH
Section 2 Crediting of Reduction Effect of Piped Renewable Gas from Abroad
|

:INFO
Art. 92d Applying for international attestations for piped renewable gas from abroad
1 An importer may apply for international attestations for the reduction effect of piped renewable gas from abroad.
2 Anyone wishing to apply for international attestations for a reduction effect must have the project in question validated at their own cost by an auditing body recognised by the FOEN.
3 The application must contain the following documents:
a. the partner state’s decision regarding the project;
b. audit report by an FOEN-recognised auditing body attesting that the requirements under Article 15 paragraph 3 of the CO 2 Act.
4 The FOEN may require additional information from the applicant if required to assess the application.
|

:INFO
Art. 92e Issuing of international attestations for piped renewable gas from abroad
1 On the basis of the application, the FOEN shall decide if the reduction effect of the piped renewable gas from abroad is suitable for international attestations to be issued.
2 If a reduction effect is deemed suitable, the FOEN shall, upon request, assess the scope of the reduction measure claimed. If necessary, it will carry out further investigations.
3 It shall issue international attestations provided that the partner country recognises the transfer of emission reductions for the reduction effect.
4 The ecological added value of the reduction effect is recognised by the attestations issued. If the added ecological value has already been offset, no attestations are issued.
5 It shall inform the applicant about the number of international attestations issued.
|

:INFO
Art. 92f Requirements for crediting the reduction effect
1 ETS participants and operators with a reduction obligation can have the reduction effect of piped renewable gas from abroad credited. They must demonstrate that:
a. piped renewable gas from abroad appears on the invoices; and
b. the FOEN has issued a sufficient number of international attestations for the reduction effect of piped renewable gas from abroad.
2 Credited international attestations for the reduction effect of piped renewable gas from abroad are credited by the FOEN to the Swiss climate target.

